  "implementation": [
    "Public recover --session runs without model/provider/credential discovery, freezes only a proven-dead original owner or repairs an existing canonical stop; live or unproven owner refuses without mutation. Exit0 requires actual later-run admission; remaining unknown returns1.",
    "Nonblocking exclusive flock on existing conversations directory is held through recovery; complete original execution control and actual device/inode identity checked before/inside writes. CLOEXEC/OS release on cancellation or process death; no mkdir lock expiry/deletion. No recovery token can dispatch.",
    "Known original per-stream aggregate fees committed exactly once independent of unresolved child cleanup. Prepared intent receives actual cancelled/not_dispatched fact only after ownership/lifecycle proof; original Grant preserved. Open approval cancellation requires original call identity, conversation/stream/capability/args and actual UUID suffix; foreign/decided approvals preserved.",
    "Known canonical Tool Result and original Grant/call/stream/args must match; missing actual Evidence is registered through the original Evidence Store before original settlement. Owner death, an existing artifact or assistant text never proves tool effect.",
    "Recorded Shell and MCP stdio group cleanup requires original complete owner/child tuples, actual PID birth/PGID and actual group absence. Local network pump termination never clears remote unknown. Starting publication gap remains blocked.",
    "Initial uncertain claim retains a sealed actual empty claim capable only of cleanup. No JSON-reopened dispatch authority; no prompt/model send or fake fees after failed admission. LockBusy cannot mint cleanup.",
    "macOS uses exact libproc0.14.11 safe BSDInfo API, real epoch seconds/microseconds and nonzero arg to include unreaped owned children. Actual Child.wait/group absence still proves stop. Own code forbids unsafe; dependency FFI separately reviewed. Old opaque display identities are not rewritten: present PID stays Unproven, actual absent PID can prove death; old native/TS consumers still require actual drain before shared default deployment."
  ],
